{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhbnPhzQBxvxiSUZ6y7y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, a single-cue model called `ideal_switch_rate_prototype`, and it passed the self-check with `OK`.\n\n**Hypothesis:** people judge how random a sequence looks by one thing — how often it switches between heads and tails. They carry an internal ideal switch rate. The closer a sequence's switch rate is to that ideal, the more random it looks. Too few switches (long streaks) and too many (perfect alternation) both make it look less random. People differ in how strongly this cue drives their choice.\n\n**Model:**\n- **Ideal rate:** fitted, with a Beta(3, 2) prior, which leans toward rates a little above one half.\n- **Randomness score:** the squared distance between a sequence's switch rate and that ideal.\n- **Sensitivity:** each person has their own, drawn from a log-normal population with 400 slots, set up the standard non-centred way so it samples well.\n- **Choice:** `p_left` is a sigmoid of the difference in distance between the right and left sequences.\n\n**Why this candidate:** the brief asked for something simpler than the existing models. This one has two population parameters plus the per-person sensitivities. It also targets the critique result that survived the multiple-comparison correction: people choose perfect alternation less often than the best model predicts (77% vs 86%). A fitted ideal rate penalises both alternation and long streaks with one mechanism. If the cue is wrong, the comparison should show it clearly.\n\n**Self-check result:** the short smoke fit (100 draws, one chain) gave an ELPD-LOO of −1028.8, close to the best model's −1023.0. Two caveats:\n- The PSIS-LOO estimate was flagged unreliable on this smoke fit: 7.9% of trials had a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance. The full admission fit could still be flagged.\n- With one chain the check can't report R-hat, so it hasn't confirmed convergence. Novelty against the other models also isn't checked yet; admission does both.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_2`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2258,"cache_read_input_tokens":51289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff579358-6de6-46c1-b0c2-eb817dc4a875","uuid":"97d276ce-9f73-4fd2-b838-a7f8bef1ab47","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:35:28.491Z","request_id":"req_011CfhbnPJRPUnfNysNjV9H4"}
